reps: 8
vscode: nothing — this muscle does not exist there
open: todo.md

@brief
Eight times: add ` done` to the end of the line, leave insert mode, save,
quit. Nothing to work out. The only goal is that the sequence stops being
a decision and becomes a reflex.

Watch `-- INSERT --` at the bottom of the screen appear and disappear.
By rep eight you should be pressing `Esc` before you have finished
thinking about it.

@keys
| `$` | end of the line |
| `a` | append after the cursor |
| `Esc` | out |
| `:wq` | save and quit |

@hints
`$a` puts you in insert mode at the very end of the line, in two keys.
--
Do not pause to check the mode indicator before pressing `Esc`. Press
`Esc` and then look. That is the reflex you want.

@solution
    $ a  done <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Vim users press `Esc` constantly, often when they are already in normal
mode, and it costs nothing. The failure mode you are drilling out is the
opposite one: typing a command like `dd` while still in insert mode and
finding the letters in your file.

If reaching for `Esc` with your little finger hurts, you are not the first.
Many people remap it later — `jk` typed quickly is the usual choice.
Chapter 27 covers mappings. Learn it the plain way first so you can sit
down at anyone's machine.

